'''OpTic Gaming''' is an [[:Category:United States|American]] esports organization known for its ''Call of Duty'', ''DOTA 2'', ''League of Legends'', ''Gears of War'' teams. The organization was also involved in the ''[[overwatch:Overwatch League|Overwatch League]]'' with ownership of the '''[[overwatch:Houston Outlaws|Houston slot]]'''. In 2017, Texas Rangers co-owner Neil Leibman acquired a majority interest in '''OpTic''', making the organisation part of '''Infinite Esports & Entertainment'''. The team is often considered the best team in the jetpack era of Call of Duty, most notably winning the 2017 Call of Duty World Champions, beating title defenders [[Team EnVyUs]] in the finals. They own [[OpTic Texas]] in the [[Call of Duty League]]. They also run the Call of Duty Challengers team [[Huntsmen]]

